.TH CUPSD.CONF 5 "2026-11-18" "yindle 0.1.1" "File Formats"
.SH NAME
cupsd.conf \- scheduler configuration file for Yindle cupsd
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.I cupsd.conf
file configures network listeners, TLS options, logging, job limits, DNS-SD
sharing, HTTP location ACLs, and IPP operation policies for
.BR cupsd (8).
It is normally located at
.I /etc/cups/cupsd.conf
with permissions
.B 0640
owned by
.BR root:lp .
.PP
Each line contains a case-insensitive directive name followed by whitespace and
its value.
Lines beginning with
.B #
and blank lines are ignored.
Paths, user/group settings, and sandboxing directives live in
.BR cups\-files.conf (5).
Validate edits before reloading with
.B cupsd \-\-check\-config
and apply without dropping connections using
.B systemctl reload cups.service
.RB ( SIGHUP ).
.SH TOP-LEVEL DIRECTIVES
.SS Network Listeners & TLS
.TP
.BI Listen " address:port" " | " /path/to/socket
Listen for HTTP/IPP connections on the specified IPv4/IPv6 address and port
(e.g.,
.BR "Listen localhost:631" )
or Unix domain socket (e.g.,
.BR "Listen /run/cups/cups.sock" ).
May be specified multiple times.
.TP
.BI Port " number"
Listen on all interfaces on TCP port
.I number
(flagged as
.B WILDCARD_LISTEN
by
.BR "cupsd \-\-check\-config" ;
prefer explicit
.B Listen
or
.B SSLListen
addresses).
.TP
.BI SSLListen " address:port"
Listen for direct TLS (IPPS/HTTPS from the first byte) on the specified address
and port.
Yindle fails closed if an explicit TLS listener cannot initialize its
certificate/key pair.
.TP
.BI SSLPort " number"
Listen for direct TLS on all interfaces on TCP port
.IR number .
.TP
.BI SSLOptions " [None] [MinTLS1.2|MinTLS1.3] [MaxTLS1.2|MaxTLS1.3] [DenyCBC]"
Configure TLS protocol bounds for
.BR rustls .
Defaults to TLS 1.2+ with AEAD cipher suites only.
Legacy protocol options
.RB ( AllowSSL3 ,
.BR MinTLS1.0 ,
.BR MinTLS1.1 ,
.BR AllowRC4 )
are rejected or flagged as
.B WEAK_TLS_OPTIONS
by
.BR "cupsd \-\-check\-config" .
.SS Server Identity
.TP
.BI ServerName " hostname"
Canonical hostname advertised in URIs and accepted in HTTP
.B Host:
headers.
.TP
.BI ServerAlias " hostname [hostname ...]"
Additional hostnames accepted in HTTP
.B Host:
headers to prevent DNS rebinding attacks.
Avoid
.B "ServerAlias *"
(flagged as
.B WILDCARD_SERVER_ALIAS
by
.BR "cupsd \-\-check\-config" ).
.TP
.BI ServerAdmin " email"
Administrator contact email address.
.TP
.BI ServerTokens " None|ProductOnly|Major|Minor|Minimal|OS|Full"
Controls verbosity of the HTTP
.B Server:
response header.
.TP
.BI HostNameLookups " On|Off|Double"
Controls reverse DNS lookup for client IP addresses (default:
.BR Off ).
.SS Logging
.TP
.BI LogLevel " none|emerg|alert|crit|error|warn|notice|info|debug|debug2"
Verbosity threshold for
.I error_log
(default:
.BR warn ).
.TP
.BI AccessLogLevel " none|config|actions|all"
Controls which HTTP/IPP requests are recorded in
.I access_log
(default:
.BR actions ).
.TP
.BI LogTimeFormat " standard|usecs"
Timestamp precision in logs (default:
.BR standard ).
.TP
.BI MaxLogSize " size"
Maximum log file size before atomic
.I .O
rotation (supports
.BR k ,
.BR m ,
.B g
suffixes; default
.B 1m
in code,
.B 0
in shipped
.I cupsd.conf.default
to delegate rotation to
.BR logrotate (8)).
.TP
.BI LogDebugHistory " count"
Number of recent debug messages retained in memory (default:
.BR 200 ).
.TP
.BI PageLogFormat " [format]"
Template for
.I page_log
entries (default:
.BR "%p %u %j %T %P %C %{job\-billing} %{job\-originating\-host\-name} %{job\-name} %{media} %{sides}" ).
An empty value disables
.I page_log
writing.
.SS Client & Connection Limits
.TP
.BI MaxClients " count"
Maximum concurrent client connections (default:
.BR 100 ).
.TP
.BI MaxClientsPerHost " count"
Maximum concurrent client connections per remote IP (default:
.BR 0 ,
meaning derived/unlimited).
.TP
.BI MaxRequestSize " size"
Maximum HTTP/IPP request body size (also accepted as
.BR LimitRequestBody ;
supports
.BR k / m / g
suffixes).
Oversized requests are rejected with HTTP
.B 413 Payload Too Large
before
.BR "100 Continue" .
.TP
.BI Timeout " seconds"
HTTP I/O timeout in seconds (default:
.BR 900 ).
.TP
.BI KeepAlive " Yes|No"
Enable or disable HTTP/1.1 persistent connections (default:
.BR Yes ).
.TP
.BI MultipleOperationTimeout " seconds"
Maximum lifetime for multi-document
.B Create\-Job
/
.B Send\-Document
sequences (default:
.BR 900 ).
.TP
.BI ReloadTimeout " seconds"
Maximum time to wait for graceful reload housekeeping (default:
.BR 30 ).
.TP
.BI DirtyCleanInterval " seconds"
Interval between persisting dirty state files to disk (default:
.BR 30 ).
.TP
.BI IdleExitTimeout " seconds"
Idle timeout before exiting in
.B \-l
on-demand mode (default:
.BR 60 ).
.SS Jobs, Queues & Filters
.TP
.BI ErrorPolicy " abort\-job|retry\-current\-job|retry\-job|stop\-printer"
Default action when a backend fails (shipped default:
.BR retry\-job ).
.TP
.BI MaxJobs " count"
Maximum total jobs kept in memory/history (default:
.BR 500 ).
.TP
.BI MaxActiveJobs " count"
Maximum simultaneously active jobs (default:
.BR 0 ,
unlimited).
.TP
.BI MaxJobsPerUser " count"
Maximum active jobs per user (default:
.BR 0 ).
.TP
.BI MaxJobsPerPrinter " count"
Maximum active jobs per printer (default:
.BR 0 ).
.TP
.BI MaxCopies " count"
Maximum copies allowed per print job (default:
.BR 9999 ).
.TP
.BI MaxJobTime " duration"
Maximum runtime for a single job before cancellation (supports
.BR m / h / d / w
suffixes; default:
.BR 10800
seconds / 3 hours).
.TP
.BI MaxHoldTime " duration"
Maximum time a job may remain held before automatic cancellation (default:
.BR 0 ).
.TP
.BI PreserveJobHistory " Yes|No|duration"
How long completed job control metadata is retained (default:
.BR Yes ).
.TP
.BI PreserveJobFiles " Yes|No|duration"
How long completed job document files
.RI ( d* )
are retained (default:
.B 86400
seconds / 1 day).
.TP
.BI AutoPurgeJobs " Yes|No"
Automatically purge completed jobs once quotas are exceeded (default:
.BR No ).
.TP
.BI JobKillDelay " seconds"
Grace period between
.B SIGTERM
and
.B SIGKILL
when canceling a running job's filter/backend process group (default:
.BR 300 ).
.TP
.BI JobRetryLimit " count"
Maximum retry attempts under
.B retry\-job
policy (default:
.BR 5 ).
.TP
.BI JobRetryInterval " seconds"
Delay between retry attempts (default:
.BR 300 ).
.TP
.BI FilterLimit " cost"
Maximum total filter cost allowed to run concurrently across all jobs (default:
.BR 0 ,
unlimited).
Exposed via Prometheus
.B yindle_filter_limit
and
.B yindle_filter_cost_current
metrics.
.TP
.BI FilterNice " 0..19"
Scheduling niceness applied to filter processes (default:
.BR 0 ).
.SS Browsing, Sharing & DNS-SD
.TP
.BI Browsing " Yes|No"
Enable or disable network printer advertising (shipped default:
.BR No ).
.TP
.BI BrowseLocalProtocols " none|dnssd|all"
Protocols used to advertise shared local printers (default:
.BR dnssd ).
.TP
.BI BrowseWebIF " Yes|No"
Advertise the web interface over DNS-SD (default:
.BR No ).
.TP
.BI BrowseIPPSOnly " Yes|No"
Advertise only TLS-protected
.B _ipps._tcp
records (default:
.BR No ).
.TP
.BI BrowseDNSSDSubTypes " _cups,_print,_universal"
Comma-separated DNS-SD subtypes advertised for AirPrint/driverless clients.
.TP
.BI DNSSDComputerName " name"
Override computer name used in DNS-SD service instances.
.TP
.BI DNSSDHostName " hostname"
Override hostname advertised in DNS-SD SRV records.
.TP
.BI DefaultShared " Yes|No"
Whether newly created queues are shared by default (shipped default:
.BR No ).
.SS Subscriptions, Auth & General
.TP
.BI DefaultAuthType " Basic|Auto|None"
Authentication scheme used when a block specifies
.B AuthType Default
(shipped default:
.BR Basic ).
.TP
.BI DefaultEncryption " Never|IfRequested|Required"
Default TLS policy when a location does not specify
.B Encryption
(default:
.BR IfRequested ).
.TP
.BI DefaultPolicy " name"
Name of the default
.B <Policy>
applied to queues without an explicit
.B OpPolicy
(default:
.BR default ).
.TP
.BI WebInterface " Yes|No"
Enable or disable HTTP access to static/CGI pages and the built-in HTML status
fallback on
.IR / ,
.IR /printers ,
.IR /classes ,
and
.I /jobs
(default:
.BR Yes ).
.TP
.BI MaxSubscriptions " count"
Maximum active RFC 3995 event subscriptions (default:
.BR 100 ).
Also supports
.BR MaxSubscriptionsPerJob ,
.BR MaxSubscriptionsPerPrinter ,
.BR MaxSubscriptionsPerUser ,
.BR DefaultLeaseDuration ,
.BR MaxLeaseDuration ,
and
.BR MaxEvents .
.TP
.BI Classification " banner"
Force a security classification banner (with optional
.BR "ClassifyOverride Yes|No" ).
.TP
.BI DefaultLanguage " locale"
Default natural language tag (default:
.BR en ).
.TP
.BI DefaultPaperSize " size"
Default media size (e.g.,
.B Letter
or
.BR A4 ).
.TP
.BI ReadyPaperSizes " size[,size...]"
Loaded media sizes reported in
.BR media\-ready .
.TP
.BI StrictConformance " Yes|No"
Require strict IPP conformance checks (default:
.BR No ).
.TP
.BI RootCertDuration " seconds"
Rotation interval for local auth certificates (default:
.BR 300 ).
.TP
.BI GSSServiceName " name"
Kerberos service principal name (parsed for compatibility; native GSSAPI
runtime adapter is on the roadmap).
.SH LOCATION AND POLICY BLOCKS
.SS <Location /path> ... </Location>
Controls HTTP/IPP access to URL prefixes
.RI ( / ,
.IR /admin ,
.IR /admin/conf ,
.IR /printers ,
.IR /jobs ,
etc.).
Canonical path normalization rejects
.BR .. ,
backslashes, and NUL bytes fail-closed.
.SS <Policy name> ... </Policy>
Defines per-operation IPP authorization rules using nested
.B "<Limit op1 op2 ...>"
or
.B "<LimitExcept op1 ...>"
blocks plus privacy directives:
.BR JobPrivateAccess ,
.BR JobPrivateValues ,
.BR SubscriptionPrivateAccess ,
and
.BR SubscriptionPrivateValues .
In Yindle, operations that do not match any
.B <Limit>
(or
.BR "<Limit All>" )
are denied fail-closed.
.SS Directives Inside Location and Limit Blocks
.TP
.BI Order " allow,deny|deny,allow"
Evaluation order for
.B Allow
and
.B Deny
host rules.
.TP
.BI Allow " [from] all|none|@LOCAL|@IF(name)|host|ip|ip/cidr|ip/mask"
Permit matching client peer addresses.
Supports IPv4, IPv6, IPv4-mapped IPv6 normalization, real local interface subnet
matching
.RB ( @LOCAL ),
and named interface matching
.RB ( @IF(eth0) ).
.TP
.BI Deny " [from] all|none|@LOCAL|@IF(name)|host|ip|ip/cidr|ip/mask"
Deny matching client peer addresses.
.B "Deny from all"
matches both IPv4 and IPv6 addresses.
.TP
.BI AuthType " None|Basic|Default|Negotiate"
Authentication requirement for this block.
.TP
.BI Encryption " IfRequested|Required|Never"
Require TLS
.RB ( Required
emits HTTP
.B 426 Upgrade Required
on plaintext connections) or permit opportunistic upgrade.
.TP
.BI Require " valid\-user | user @OWNER @SYSTEM name ... | group name ..."
Restrict access to authenticated users, job owners
.RB ( @OWNER ),
configured
.B SystemGroup
administrators
.RB ( @SYSTEM ),
or Unix groups.
.TP
.BI Satisfy " all|any"
Controls whether
.B both
host ACL and authentication rules must pass
.RB ( all )
or either one suffices
.RB ( any ).
.B Security note:
Yindle intentionally defaults to
.B "Satisfy all"
(differing from upstream CUPS's
.B "Satisfy any"
default) so empty host ACLs cannot bypass
.BR "Require user @SYSTEM" .
.SH EXAMPLES
Minimal hardened loopback configuration:
.PP
.EX
LogLevel warn
MaxLogSize 0
ErrorPolicy retry\-job
Listen localhost:631
Listen /run/cups/cups.sock
Browsing No
DefaultAuthType Basic
DefaultShared No
WebInterface Yes

<Location />
  Order allow,deny
  Allow from @LOCAL
</Location>

<Location /admin>
  AuthType Default
  Require user @SYSTEM
  Satisfy all
  Order allow,deny
  Allow from @LOCAL
</Location>
.EE
.SH FILES
.I /etc/cups/cupsd.conf
.br
.I /etc/cups/cupsd.conf.default
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cupsd (8),
.BR cups\-files.conf (5),
.BR cupsfilter (8),
.BR cups\-lpd (8)
